    "detail": "the reference (schematic) and extracted netlists instantiate the same device models/`.subckt`s and differ only in how many instances of each they carry. The usual cause is finger/multiplier decomposition: the layout draws a device as several fingers while the schematic has one instance (with `nf`/`m`, or none), a difference `klt lvs` has already reconciled. It does not by itself make `delta[]` unrelated, but representation effects (fingering, AS/AD) are folded into `delta[]` alongside the parasitics. See docs/cli/pex.md's `model_mismatch` section"
